1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,025
Your phone says twenty percent. Then it
dies in a minute.

2
00:00:05,575 --> 00:00:09,817
The gauge reads twenty percent. The cell
is nearly empty.

3
00:00:11,367 --> 00:00:15,602
You blame a dying cell. The problem is a
lying gauge.

4
00:00:16,572 --> 00:00:20,741
The gauge reads voltage, and voltage sags
under load.

5
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:24,566
A cheap cable drops the voltage.

6
00:00:25,536 --> 00:00:28,640
Cold weather slows the reaction inside the
cell.

7
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:32,171
A three year old cell simply holds less.

8
00:00:33,721 --> 00:00:37,194
Forty five percent of the error is voltage
sag.

9
00:00:38,164 --> 00:00:39,559
Twenty is cold.

10
00:00:40,529 --> 00:00:42,063
Thirty five is age.

11
00:00:43,613 --> 00:00:44,737
Run one check.

12
00:00:45,707 --> 00:00:47,391
It is called battery health.

13
00:00:48,941 --> 00:00:52,899
Check the cable first. It is the cheapest
of the three.
